.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1211 AM PDT Fri Aug 7 2026
(Friday through Sunday)

Upper-level ridging across the Four Corners will expand westward
Friday. Areas of moderate HeatRisk across the interior on Friday
will expand to become widespread on Saturday and Sunday with areas
of major HeatRisk. Saturday and Sunday will be the hottest days of
the week with temperatures 10-15 degrees above normal. Subsidence
aloft will compress the 1,000 foot marine layer, keeping relief
confined to the immediate coast. Near-critical fire weather
conditions persist through the weekend across the interior due to
very hot and dry conditions. Minor coastal flooding is expected
during the highest high tide (evening/overnight) for bayshore
locations along the San Francisco Bay, San Pablo Bay, and Monterey
Bay Friday evening through Thursday morning. The Pacific Coast may
need to be added Sunday through Tuesday, it will depend on how the
positive anomaly performs leading up to it.

&&

.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1211 AM PDT Fri Aug 7 2026
(Monday through Thursday)

Global ensemble clusters are in agreement that upper-level shortwave
troughing will develop Monday off the West Coast between subtropical
high pressure across the Eastern Pacific Ocean and the Four Corners
high. This will result in temperatures moderating to near normal and
the return of a marine layer around 1,000 feet. The surface pressure
gradient will support northerly winds across the waters that will be
hazardous to small craft.

